WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.567
Week 9: Daily Routine and Reflexive Verbs. sequence a routine say what is happening now compare schedules

2
00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:14.729
Form and meaning. Reflexive pronouns; routines; antes de/después de; present progressive.

3
00:00:14.729 --> 00:00:38.449
Model set. Me levanto a las seis y media. Después de vestirme, preparo el desayuno. Ahora estoy esperando el tren. Los niños se acuestan temprano. ¿A qué hora te despiertas? I get up at six thirty. After getting dressed, I prepare breakfast. I am waiting for the train now. The children go to bed early. What time do you wake up?

4
00:00:38.449 --> 00:00:48.664
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:48.664 --> 00:01:00.650
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: sequence a routine; say what is happening now; compare schedules. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:25.116
Model language. Me levanto a las seis y media. — I get up at six thirty. Después de vestirme, preparo el desayuno. — After getting dressed, I prepare breakfast. Ahora estoy esperando el tren. — I am waiting for the train now. Los niños se acuestan temprano. — The children go to bed early. ¿A qué hora te despiertas? — What time do you wake up?

7
00:01:25.116 --> 00:01:35.035
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
